	When you're unskilled with a weapon, you're at -4 to hit
and -2 to damage.  For low-level non-combat wombats, this is brutal.  

	I go up to level 1 to practice with a new weapon.  Or, if 
training up in the new weapon isn't a priority, I only wield it
against slow monsters, where I can spend as long as I want on hack-
and-back.

	(When playing a wizard, do this with daggers.  The gnomish
mages in minetown are very good for this:  they rarely hurt you
faster than you heal, and you can mindlessly slash away.  Don't
enhance your dagger skill until you need to throw daggers in a fight;
you do less damage when unskilled, but you still get credits towards
advancing the skill a second time.  Your sparring partner gives you
more practice before he disintegrates.  IIRC, I once jumped directly
from Unskilled to Expert.)


> Is a healer really untenable without a pet?

